  "method": "Written by Claude (an LLM, Opus 5.5) in one session, after reading all 14 corpus files in full at corpus_commit and before any search was run over them. Each query was written from what a section is for (the intent a reader would bring), and its relevant passages were marked at the same time by reading, never from search output. Grade 2: the passage answers the query; grade 1: it is relevant but partial or a passing mention. The split was fixed when the file was written: within each style, queries alternate tune / heldout in file order. Paraphrase queries share no BM25 term with any grade-2 passage (checked by the tests). The file was committed before the first search over the corpus, and labels are not edited after looking at results.",
  "sets": {
    "1": "the queries without a \"set\" field, written as described in method",
    "2": "Added later by Claude (an LLM, Opus 5.5) in another session, because set 1's two halves had informed several decisions (chunk size, phrase weight, coverage-weighted fusion). Written after reading all 14 corpus files in full at corpus_commit and before any search with these queries; relevant passages were marked by reading, never from search output. The author knew set 1's aggregate results and the next hypothesis to test (a weight for the vector side of hybrid fusion), a possible bias that the held-out half and BEIR are there to check. Needs that set 1 already covers were avoided. Same styles, grades and rules as set 1; the split alternates tune / heldout within each style of set 2 in file order, starting with tune. Two paraphrases were reworded before the commit to pass the no-shared-term test. Committed before the first search; labels are not edited after looking at results."
  },
